     "definition": "Diffuse lights are accumulated in monochrome and then alpha-blended with diffuse map and diffuse detail map. The color is determined by double-multiplying both maps and multiplying with the accumulated light, the result being alpha-blended into the framebuffer. The opacity is determined by multiplying both map's alpha channels. Since this effect is alpha-blended, it covers up tinting and reflection on pixels with high opacity."
